\sendlines sends every line executed in the current pane
via OSC to another LiveLily, which receives them with
\fromosc. Messages are sent to port 9050.
It takes two arguments, the IP of the receiving computer
and the number of its pane (counting from 1):

\sendlines 192.168.1.20 1

Each executed line is sent as a string to the address
/livelily1/press, and its characters are typed in the
first pane of the receiving LiveLily.
There is no option to stop sending lines.

To send every key as it is typed, use \sendkeys.
